From: Antigravity Autonomous Agent <engineering@lenovo-d330-fix.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/dsi: pulse the DSI-block MIPIO reset on resume for the Lenovo IdeaPad D330 panel

The Lenovo IdeaPad D330-10IGL (82H0) panel stays black after S3 resume, while
unbind/bind (full PCI re-probe) always lights it. Phase-48 iteration 2
(RESUME_FIX_LEDGER row 31) proved the panel-side power rails now behave like
the reload path (the wake state became backlit-but-blank instead of dark),
which leaves the DSI-block hardware reset as the remaining pre-TCON host
difference: the reload's power-well cycle drops the DSI-block MIPIO reset
control and brings the DSI block up from reset before any sequence runs,
while the resume path never pulses that control (the code block that
programs it is broxton-only in vlv_dsi.c and is skipped on this Gemini Lake
machine).

DMI-gated to 82H0, at the very top of intel_dsi_pre_enable() (before the
iteration-2 block, before intel_dsi_wait_panel_power_cycle() and the PLL
work), and only inside the power-domain init/resume window
(display->power.domains.init_wakeref, the same resume gate the iteration-2
patch established), drop the MIPIO_RST_CTRL bit of BXT_P_CR_GT_DISP_PWRON
(the DSI block held in reset, the power-well-off state), dwell 10 ms,
re-assert the bit (the block released, the state the enable path leaves it
in), dwell 10 ms, then let the existing flow run.

Control flow only: the MIPIO_RST_CTRL toggle is a reset-domain control
write, not a value restore; the banned operational-offset list does not
cover this PWRON control register.

Requires the iteration-2 patch (patches/d330_dsi_panel_power_cycle.patch)
applied first: this patch reuses its d330_82h0_panel() DMI helper, and its
hunk context is the post-iteration-2 file.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity Autonomous Agent <engineering@lenovo-d330-fix.local>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/vlv_dsi.c
@@ -753,5 +753,30 @@
 	drm_dbg_kms(display->drm, "\n");
 
+	/*
+	 * Lenovo IdeaPad D330-10IGL (82H0): the reload path (unbind/bind)
+	 * goes through the display power-well cycle, which drops the
+	 * DSI-block MIPIO reset control and brings the DSI block up from
+	 * reset before any sequence runs. The resume path never pulses
+	 * that control (the code block that programs it is broxton-only,
+	 * skipped on this Gemini Lake machine), so the DSI block starts
+	 * the resume sequence from its retained state. Pulse it the way
+	 * the power-well cycle does: drop MIPIO_RST_CTRL (block held in
+	 * reset), dwell, re-assert it (block released, the state the
+	 * enable path leaves it in), then let the existing flow run.
+	 *
+	 * Control flow only: a reset-domain toggle; no operational
+	 * register values are written.
+	 */
+	if (d330_82h0_panel() &&
+	    display->power.domains.init_wakeref) {
+		drm_info(display->drm,
+			 "[D330 82H0] resume: MIPIO reset pulse before DSI init\n");
+		intel_de_rmw(display, BXT_P_CR_GT_DISP_PWRON, MIPIO_RST_CTRL, 0);
+		msleep(10);
+		intel_de_rmw(display, BXT_P_CR_GT_DISP_PWRON, 0, MIPIO_RST_CTRL);
+		msleep(10);
+	}
+
